   "text": "[Verse 1]  \nIn a cozy little room, where the sun shines bright,  \nLived a corgi named Max with a heart so bright.  \nHe’d bark at the mail, with a cheerful tone,  \nBut his love was more than just a bark or tone.  \n\n[Verse 2]  \nMax loved to play, with a grin that could shine,  \nHe’d chase the shadows, and then come back to dine.  \nHis tail would wag, with a rhythm so true,  \nA song that only he could truly know.  \n\n[Chorus]  \nMax the corgi, with a spirit so true,  \nHe’d dance in the rain, with a heart so full.  \nFrom the kitchen to the yard, he’d make it all fun,  \nA loyal friend, with a love that’s unbound.  \n\n[Verse 3]  \nHe’d cuddle the cat, with a gentle touch,  \nAnd he’d nudge the dog with a playful look.  \nHis love was in every small, quiet act,  \nA bond that only he could truly craft.  \n\n[Chorus]  \nMax the corgi, with a spirit so true,  \nHe’d dance in the rain, with a heart so full.  \nFrom the kitchen to the yard, he’d make it all fun,  \nA loyal friend, with a love that’s unbound.  \n\n[Outro]  \nSo here’s to Max, the corgi with a heart so wide,  \nA life filled with love, and a joy that’s so wide.",
